WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.340
High-performance chips are needed to build
our future: whether it’s for artificial

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.940
intelligence or driverless cars.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:12.510
The key to producing advanced chips is by
generating Extreme Ultraviolet light.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:17.630
EUV light is revolutionary because it has
a much shorter wavelength compared to visible

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.630
light.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:24.400
This allows EUV light to create extremely
small structures on chips - circuitry that’s

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.840
10,000 times thinner than a strand of a human
hair!

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.810
The more structures that are packed onto a
chip, the more powerful the chip becomes.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:38.110
The thing is - EUV light does NOT occur naturally
here on Earth - it’s only found in outer

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.110
space.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:42.000
So, how do you generate EUV light on earth?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.559
That’s where a powerful laser comes into
play.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:47.820
A TRUMPF laser from Germany.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.110
No, it has nothing to do with the former U.S.
president.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:57.480
This high-powered laser strikes tiny droplets
of the metal tin in a vacuum chamber as they

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.660
shoot past.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:05.460
We’re talking about striking 50,000 droplets
of tin in just one second!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.600
The giant laser takes two shots at each droplet.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.700
The first flattens the tin.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.180
The second, bigger pulse vaporizes the tin,
creating a plasma that generates the prized

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:22.299
EUV light upon impact, at the desired wavelength
of 13.5 nanometers.

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:25.850
Light is projected through a blueprint of
the pattern that will be printed.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:30.619
In a previous video, I explained how mirrors
made by the German company, ZEISS, focus the

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:34.840
pattern onto the silicon wafer, which has
already been coated with a light-sensitive

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.869
chemical.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:40.259
The wafer is eventually split into little
pieces of microchips.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:46.170
No other laser on the market can hit 50,000
droplets per second at precisely the right

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.170
moment.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:52.299
Not a moment too soon or too late - otherwise,
the impact will not flatten the tin droplet.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:57.470
So TRUMPF’s light beam must be shaped in
a very specific way.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:02.460
Each laser pulse consists of a small, compact
group of light particles hurled at the tin

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.759
droplets in a tight bunch.

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:08.239
The plasma that is generated is extremely
hot.

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:15.700
With a temperature of 220,000 degrees Celsius
(or 396,000 degrees Fahrenheit) - which is

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.950
30 to 40 times hotter than the surface of
the sun.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:25.340
The TRUMPF laser is used in the Dutch firm
ASML’s huge machines that perform the crucial

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:30.849
step in the chipmaking process: of printing
tiny patterns - circuitry - on silicon wafers.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:36.739
ASML is the only company that is currently
capable of building the world’s most advanced

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:41.129
system needed to print chips: its EUV lithography
system.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:47.830
It’s less advanced machines, Deep UV lithography
systems, can still print quality chips - just

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.690
not the most sophisticated kind.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:54.360
Think of it this way: if somebody were to
write their name with a highlighter in smaller

00:02:54.360 --> 00:03:00.900
and smaller writing, in ever smaller writing,
you would eventually need a different pen

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.480
to write even smaller.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.659
EUV machines are like a finer pen.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:12.080
If you own a relatively new smartphone or
smartwatch, you’ve likely benefitted from

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.760
EUV lithography technology.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:20.000
So far, China has NOT been able to get its
hands on these sophisticated machines.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.810
When President Trump was in office, he pressed
the Dutch government not to sell the most

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.950
advanced machines to China.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:31.220
The Biden administration has continued putting
pressure on ASML amid the ongoing chip war

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.319
with China.

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:37.950
Washington’s sanctions in October ban U.S.
citizens, permanent residents, and green card

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:43.530
holders from supporting the development or
production of advanced chips at certain factories

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.810
in China - which could affect hundreds of
people working for Chinese semiconductor companies.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.409
And perhaps - it could force them to choose
between their citizenship or their job.

00:03:53.409 --> 00:04:00.040
As a result, ASML sent out a memo in October
instructing its U.S. employees to stop servicing

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.720
Chinese customers.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.090
The memo says they “are prohibited from
providing certain services to advanced fabs

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.090
in China.”

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.360
until further notice.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.200
A fab refers to a chip manufacturing plant.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:17.389
ASML has several locations in China for research
and development, manufacturing, and training.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:23.510
However, at present, it does NOT sell its
most advanced EUV systems that use the TRUMPF

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.910
lasers to China.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:30.780
So, a tightly connected group of European
companies rule the technological world, in

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.039
many ways.

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:37.120
The Dutch company ASML is the only company
that manufactures advanced machines to build

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.590
the circuitry for high-end chips.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:45.110
It relies on TRUMPF lasers to generate EUV
light to pattern the finest lines on microchips.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:50.280
And mirrors from the German company ZEISS
collect and focus the EUV light.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.170
I’ve done videos on all three companies
which I’ll link to in my description.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:05:00.980
Other chipmakers then use their EUV systems
to manufacture their own microchips: Intel,

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.419
Samsung, and TSMC.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:08.240
Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company
makes nearly ALL of the world’s most advanced

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.240
chips.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:15.070
TSMC currently produces 5-nanometer chips
and is striving for next-generation, 3-nanometer

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.070
ones.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:22.580
So, when we talk about the future of tech,
TRUMPF, ZEISS, and ASML are critical pieces

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:27.419
of a puzzle that together are shaping the
world of tomorrow.

